{"Hardcoded refresh_token placeholder breaks token preservation - sets refresh_token to literal string 'refresh_token' when missing, contradicting commit 358aa8be2's pattern to preserve old tokens, causing OAuth providers to reject this invalid token string": 0.9362410306930542, "Invalid Zod schema syntax in parseRefreshTokenResponse - uses z.string().toString() as object keys, which evaluates to the literal string '[object Object]' instead of creating dynamic key validation, causing token validation to fail for credential sync mode": 0.8854948282241821, "Google Calendar stores entire parse result instead of extracted data - stores the entire SafeParseReturnType object {success: boolean, data: any} to the database instead of extracting .data like other integrations (Zoom, Office365, Salesforce)": 0.9543779492378235, "Salesforce integration missing refreshOAuthTokens wrapper - unlike all other integrations (Google Calendar, Office365, Zoom, Hubspot, etc.), Salesforce makes a direct fetch() call instead of using the refreshOAuthTokens() wrapper, which means it will bypass the custom sync endpoint even when APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED is true": 0.9784839153289795, "Zoho-Bigin passes wrong parameter type to refreshOAuthTokens - passes credentialId (credential's database ID) instead of credential.userId, causing the sync endpoint to receive the wrong identifier": 0.9523380994796753, "Salesforce integration uses stale credentials after token refresh - after refreshing tokens and updating the database with new tokens from accessTokenParsed.data, the code creates a jsforce.Connection using the OLD credentialKey values instead of the newly refreshed tokens, causing immediate API failures": 0.9308362603187561}